course: dictionary
lesson: 9358
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word spoil has several meanings, so the words around it tell you which one is right. To spoil something means to ruin it or make it worse. «Cheating spoils a game, because nobody can trust the result.» Nobody can trust a game that is cheated, so spoils must mean ruins.
explain: Spoil can also mean giving a child everything they want, so they expect too much. Look for clues. A spoiled child sulks when they don't get their way. The clues point to too much giving, not to ruining.
explain: Spoil can even mean to treat someone kindly in a special way. When you meet spoil, ask: which meaning fits here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Spoil means to ruin something or make it worse.
fact: Food spoils when it goes bad and is no longer safe to eat.
fact: To spoil a child means to give them everything they want, so they may expect too much.
fact: A spoiler tells the ending of a story, and so it spoils the surprise.
fact: A spoilsport is a person who spoils other people's fun.
exercise: «Cheating spoils a game, because nobody can trust the result.» What does spoils mean here? | Makes it longer | Starts it again quickly | Tidies it up neatly | *Ruins it, making it worse
exercise: Mum says, «The milk has spoiled, so don't drink it.» What does spoiled mean? | *Gone bad and not safe to eat | Full to the top | Very cold and fresh | Left in the sun to dry
exercise: Priya says, «Don't read the last page, it will spoil the ending.» What does spoil the ending mean? | Make the story longer | Make it end on a happy note | *Tell it and take away the surprise | Read it twice
test: «Grandma will spoil you with cakes and sweets.» What does spoil mean here? | Hurt you with sharp knives | Put you to bed early | Make you cry | *Give you lots of treats so you expect too much
test: «In a film, rustling wrappers can spoil things for others.» What does spoil mean here? | Turn the lights on | *Ruin the fun and calm for people nearby | Make the film longer | Pack the wrappers neatly
exam: «Dad said the fish would spoil if we left it out of the fridge.» What does spoil mean here? | *Go bad and stop being safe to eat | Freeze solid | Grow bigger | Swim away
